WEBVTT

00:03.758 --> 00:07.389
<i>Fuko and Andy succeed in contacting Anno Un.</i>

00:07.641 --> 00:10.730
<i>Anno tells them that he wants
to help them become stronger.</i>

00:10.813 --> 00:14.988
<i>Fuko and Andy end up fighting against Autumn
to save a man assaulted by the UMA.</i>

00:15.489 --> 00:19.080
<i>However, they are unable to win against Autumn
at their current skill level.</i>

00:19.163 --> 00:23.463
<i>Drawing up Andy's arm with G-Liner,
Anno uses it to release a powerful attack</i>

00:23.463 --> 00:25.927
<i>and shows them the potential of Negator abilities.</i>

00:26.052 --> 00:28.891
<i>However, not even that is enough to defeat Autumn,</i>

00:28.891 --> 00:33.191
<i>so the trio retreat from the battle against Autumn
and head to Anno's mansion.</i>

00:33.191 --> 00:36.532
<i>There, they convince Juiz
to allow Anno to train the pair,</i>

00:36.615 --> 00:39.412
<i>transforming Andy into a giant book
that reaches up into outer space.</i>

00:41.374 --> 00:42.209
Huh?

00:42.585 --> 00:45.340
It's massive!
Why's it so large?

00:45.340 --> 00:48.305
Most likely because Victor's portion is included.

00:48.681 --> 00:52.772
Basically, this is how long he's actually lived.

00:53.231 --> 00:57.072
So all I have to do is read this
to learn about Andy's past?

00:57.072 --> 00:58.074
Nah.

00:58.951 --> 00:59.619
You'll go in.

01:00.329 --> 01:01.289
Go in?

01:01.707 --> 01:03.878
I mean, you can't read something this big, right?

01:04.462 --> 01:06.299
It's too heavy to even open.

01:06.299 --> 01:08.679
But what do you mean, I'll go in?

01:09.806 --> 01:13.021
How'd you expect to pull off something akin
to a fairy tale-

01:13.564 --> 01:14.273
Hmm?

01:14.566 --> 01:16.987
Huh? Is that... me?

01:16.987 --> 01:18.616
Nothing to panic over, Fuko.

01:20.578 --> 01:23.208
Artifact: Soul Caliber.

01:23.751 --> 01:28.176
It can pluck out people's souls,
and seal them inside of objects.

01:28.176 --> 01:31.391
I'm going to have you go inside that book.

01:40.660 --> 01:44.543
There, you'll learn parts about him unknown to you,
and learn more about yourself.

01:45.168 --> 01:49.385
And he will also gain a deeper understanding of you,
and reexamine his own past.

01:49.385 --> 01:50.972
What? What do you mean?

01:51.264 --> 01:52.474
In other words...

01:53.686 --> 01:55.313
...you'll find out!

01:55.857 --> 01:58.486
Why Andy was born, that is!

03:41.233 --> 03:42.945
Where am I?

03:43.363 --> 03:45.367
Am I already in Andy's memories?

03:47.329 --> 03:48.582
Freeze!

03:50.293 --> 03:52.381
One of the kids that got away?
Get back 'ere!

03:52.381 --> 03:58.476
My name is Izumo Fuko! Err, I mean,
"Fuko Izumo! Japanese!"

03:58.560 --> 04:01.608
Huh? Ya wanna die?
Speak English!

04:01.817 --> 04:04.614
Huh? I can't use Mr. Nico's necktie here?

04:05.115 --> 04:12.379
"I-I'm normal 18! No dangerous!
Don't touch me, okay?"

04:14.466 --> 04:16.847
I should've studied more English!

04:23.443 --> 04:25.948
Sanders! Josh! Red!

04:26.323 --> 04:28.787
You tellin' me you didn't save all the kids?

04:29.079 --> 04:32.670
No, I made sure!
The kids don't know who she is!

04:32.920 --> 04:33.756
What?

04:35.593 --> 04:37.638
A-Andy?

04:38.139 --> 04:38.974
Huh?

04:39.475 --> 04:41.312
Andy? That's you, isn't it, Andy?

04:41.855 --> 04:43.525
Where are we? And when?

04:44.026 --> 04:46.573
We're only a little ways out from Longing.

04:46.573 --> 04:49.369
You're speaking Japanese.
You from there?

04:49.871 --> 04:55.966
Omigod, I knew I could count on you, Andy!
You could speak Japanese since this era!

04:56.425 --> 04:59.348
Who's this "Andy" you've been going on about?

04:59.348 --> 05:02.270
Oh, right!
You had a different name at this point!

05:03.857 --> 05:06.696
Just how long are y'gonna stay latched to the captain?

05:06.696 --> 05:09.368
Huh? You can speak Japanese, too.

05:09.619 --> 05:10.579
Josh?

05:13.292 --> 05:15.380
My hair didn't touch you just now, did it?

05:15.714 --> 05:18.929
Oh, no, what now?
A stroke of unluck is on the way!

05:20.056 --> 05:23.271
Unluck? What are you talking about?

05:27.362 --> 05:30.118
Oh, geez!
At least it was just a light stroke!

05:32.414 --> 05:37.675
You just predicted that, didn't you?
You a witch? You must be.

05:37.675 --> 05:39.554
- All right, better kill you.
- Eek!

05:40.138 --> 05:43.770
<i>Crap, crap.
I just found Andy, but I'm gonna die!</i>

05:44.146 --> 05:46.860
<i>Gotta explain!
Gotta earn their trust!</i>

05:49.616 --> 05:52.120
"Left shoulder, Dead End."

05:52.245 --> 05:55.878
"Left chest, 1865!"

05:56.588 --> 05:59.677
"My name is Fuko Izumo."

05:59.677 --> 06:01.806
"I know your future!"

06:02.224 --> 06:05.021
Why does this girl know about your tattoos, Captain?

06:07.108 --> 06:11.241
Say what? What kinda relationship
d'you have with the captain? Well?

06:15.458 --> 06:16.418
C'mon.

06:19.091 --> 06:20.511
Let's go eat.

06:30.280 --> 06:32.117
Daddy!

06:32.117 --> 06:33.452
I'm glad you were all right.

06:38.045 --> 06:43.807
Thank you so much for saving the children.
Please let me repay you in some fashion.

06:50.153 --> 06:52.742
Um... you speak Japanese well.

06:52.742 --> 06:54.746
Yeah, the captain taught me!

06:54.954 --> 06:59.589
I wanna go meet some samurai!
And learn how to quick-draw!

07:05.475 --> 07:08.481
Are you sure? You only want food?

07:08.899 --> 07:12.656
Yeah, I don't mind.
Just food and booze for now.

07:12.948 --> 07:16.956
If you like, we have plenty
of this town's famous local brew.

07:16.956 --> 07:19.545
Although it might be a little too strong for outsiders.

07:19.545 --> 07:21.841
Bring it on. Let's have a contest!

07:21.841 --> 07:23.553
- Hell yeah, count us in!
- Hell yeah, count us in!

07:47.518 --> 07:50.022
So what do you guys normally do?

07:50.481 --> 07:54.657
A lot of places are in bad shape now that
the Civil War's over.

07:54.657 --> 07:56.786
So we beat up fools up to no good...

07:57.621 --> 08:01.253
...and get thanked like this as we wander about.

08:02.005 --> 08:04.677
<i>The Civil War? What year was that, again?</i>

08:04.886 --> 08:08.017
That's just a front and you know it.
We know the real deal.

08:09.687 --> 08:14.822
Captain doesn't remember his past.
That's why he's been roaming around the world.

08:15.239 --> 08:19.665
He's been hoping to run into someone
who knows who he is.

08:22.546 --> 08:26.554
Us three were saved from trouble over
the course of his journey.

08:26.554 --> 08:28.265
Now we're helpin' him the best we can.

08:29.059 --> 08:30.144
So, y'know...

08:31.689 --> 08:35.530
You better not be lying about knowing the captain...

08:35.530 --> 08:36.574
- Or you're dead meat.
- Or you're dead meat.

08:38.662 --> 08:43.546
Settle down, guys.
She won't tell us anything with threats like that.

08:44.381 --> 08:49.266
Fuko, right?
How do you know about my tattoos?

08:49.767 --> 08:51.270
"How"?

08:53.608 --> 08:56.781
In the future, you're always naked...

08:58.367 --> 08:59.119
Huh?

09:01.123 --> 09:02.668
I'd never do that.

09:02.710 --> 09:03.837
I'm not lying!

09:04.254 --> 09:07.427
I don't know.
But you've lived as Undead for so long,

09:07.427 --> 09:11.059
maybe it warped your values for that kinda stuff.

09:11.435 --> 09:15.151
Oh, and also, in the future,
you used a katana!

09:17.196 --> 09:18.365
And you used your fingers as a gun to-

09:18.449 --> 09:19.326
Wait, back up.

09:19.660 --> 09:20.787
Undead?

09:20.787 --> 09:21.789
Yes.

09:22.916 --> 09:23.585
Huh?

09:26.549 --> 09:30.641
Captain's wounds do heal lickety-split,
but he ain't immortal!

09:31.224 --> 09:32.477
<i>I get it.</i>

09:32.477 --> 09:35.609
<i>Andy in this era isn't aware
that he's Undead yet.</i>

09:37.487 --> 09:41.119
Andy... let me join your crew.

09:44.877 --> 09:48.258
Nothing I say now will make you trust me, right?

09:48.551 --> 09:51.849
Then let me risk my life right alongside you
on your journey.

09:52.266 --> 09:56.651
I can gain your trust, get stronger,
and learn more about you, Andy.

09:56.651 --> 09:57.945
It's killing three birds with one stone.

10:14.436 --> 10:16.398
Loaded one bullet.

10:17.943 --> 10:20.156
Aim it at your head and pull.

10:20.156 --> 10:22.410
If you live,
I'll let you join my crew.

10:24.623 --> 10:27.671
Nice. First induction test in a while.

10:52.721 --> 10:53.848
Youch!

10:53.848 --> 10:55.434
Are you outta your damn mind?

10:55.434 --> 10:56.896
I'm sorry!

10:57.480 --> 10:58.357
But...

10:58.650 --> 11:00.570
It wasn't loaded, right?

11:02.908 --> 11:05.705
You did do a good job tricking me,
so I couldn't tell.

11:07.834 --> 11:14.472
Even if it's only a one-in-six chance,
the Andy I know wouldn't do that to a non-fighter.

11:16.017 --> 11:19.482
Thank goodness.
I guess you're still the same Andy after all.

11:22.573 --> 11:25.494
What would you have done
if there actually was a bullet in there?

11:25.494 --> 11:27.666
Oh, it'd have been fine.
It's Andy!

11:27.666 --> 11:29.377
Uh, sure, but what if?

11:29.377 --> 11:30.839
Just fine.

11:32.759 --> 11:34.220
Welp, anyway, I like ya.

11:34.889 --> 11:37.101
I say we let her join the gang.

11:37.769 --> 11:38.938
Right? Captain-

11:51.756 --> 11:53.175
They all dead?

11:53.175 --> 11:53.760
Yep.

11:54.135 --> 11:56.139
That was light work.

11:56.891 --> 11:58.728
Hey, saloon woman.

11:59.228 --> 12:04.782
Ya did good. Ya got 'em plenty drunk just like
we planned. Made it easy for us.

12:04.782 --> 12:07.871
R-Right. So, like you promised-

12:07.871 --> 12:11.211
Yeah. We won't mess with the kids anymore.

12:18.893 --> 12:20.522
Fuko...

12:20.522 --> 12:25.990
Ms. Josh... you protected me.

12:26.659 --> 12:30.082
In the future, the captain...
he doin' well?

12:31.167 --> 12:34.132
He doesn't look like... he's in pain?

12:34.132 --> 12:37.013
No! He's fine. Great, in fact!

12:39.100 --> 12:40.310
Great...

12:42.022 --> 12:43.316
Glad to hear it...

12:46.615 --> 12:48.661
Sanders, I'll be borrowing these.

12:49.913 --> 12:51.374
I'll be right back.

12:52.168 --> 12:53.086
Andy!

12:54.506 --> 12:57.470
<i>What learning about Andy meant...</i>

12:59.432 --> 13:00.142
<i>It meant...</i>

13:01.478 --> 13:04.233
<i>...learning about the numerous farewells.</i>

13:06.196 --> 13:12.584
I see. Now that I know that I'm Undead,
melee attacks make more sense.

13:13.168 --> 13:17.009
If I ain't gonna die,
I could care less about the pain.

13:20.683 --> 13:24.357
<i>So it's my duty to witness each one
with my own eyes.</i>

13:41.307 --> 13:43.646
Sorry I made you give me a hand.

13:44.188 --> 13:47.278
No, it's fine. I had to do this.

13:48.405 --> 13:50.660
Ms. Josh saved me.

13:51.369 --> 13:56.170
The three of 'em were good people.
Far too good for me, in fact.

13:57.047 --> 13:57.924
Pardon...

13:58.593 --> 14:02.517
This is my fault for following their plan.

14:02.517 --> 14:05.063
And we were in your debt, too.

14:05.690 --> 14:11.117
I'll atone for it all!
So, please... forgive the others!

14:12.244 --> 14:13.956
Ms. Saloon Manager...

14:13.956 --> 14:14.958
I see.

14:17.421 --> 14:20.887
Wait, Andy! She didn't do it because she wanted to.

14:20.887 --> 14:21.680
Let go.

14:35.792 --> 14:41.052
Pour out booze that Anhueser's selling on their graves,
every year on this day

14:41.052 --> 14:43.683
and every time they release a new one.

14:44.475 --> 14:47.649
Till the day you die.
And don't you skip a single time.

14:48.609 --> 14:52.491
Do that, and those three won't blame ya
for what ya did.

14:53.451 --> 14:57.251
Yes! I will.
I swear to God!

15:00.257 --> 15:01.384
Let's go.

15:01.384 --> 15:02.219
Okay.

15:11.947 --> 15:13.241
You sure are kind.

15:13.241 --> 15:14.578
How so?

15:14.578 --> 15:17.249
That lady was a very kind person...

15:17.959 --> 15:20.297
...she would've kept blaming herself.

15:20.297 --> 15:22.301
So you gave her a way to make amends-

15:22.301 --> 15:23.929
You're giving me too much credit.

15:24.848 --> 15:26.810
I just want her to suffer.

15:27.604 --> 15:29.775
Nothing more, nothing less.

15:31.444 --> 15:32.488
I see.

15:33.908 --> 15:37.247
So is it okay to assume I joined your crew now?

15:37.247 --> 15:40.880
Huh? Whatcha talkin' about?
I'm dropping you off at a town nearby.

15:40.880 --> 15:43.886
Hold on! That wasn't part of the deal!
I passed your test, didn't I?

15:43.886 --> 15:45.556
All right, then the crew is disbanded.

15:45.556 --> 15:47.392
Wait a second!

15:51.192 --> 15:54.616
<i>From then on,
I traveled with Andy on his journey.</i>

15:55.827 --> 16:00.878
<i>We ran into and parted ways
with many people in many places.</i>

16:01.797 --> 16:06.515
<i>It felt like eons had passed,
but it also felt like a blink of an eye.</i>

16:07.684 --> 16:11.315
<i>It felt similar to when I have dreams.</i>

16:12.276 --> 16:17.704
<i>It was a strange experience-
like I'd become a character in some sort of book.</i>

16:18.831 --> 16:23.089
<i>But during all that time,
Andy never cracked a smile.</i>

16:24.049 --> 16:28.474
<i>And he never once talked about his past.</i>

16:32.984 --> 16:35.405
"Luck Negator"?

16:36.282 --> 16:38.579
What're you talking about, Ms. Fuko?

16:38.579 --> 16:39.831
Hmm...

16:40.123 --> 16:43.797
<i>It'd be dangerous if I didn't fill in
the newcomers, I guess.</i>

16:45.635 --> 16:49.559
<i>If we get to know each other first,
I'd seriously injure them.</i>

16:50.561 --> 16:52.356
One stroke of unluck, coming up.

17:00.748 --> 17:04.421
Welp, that does it for the rite of passage.
I'll go bring Andy his food!

17:04.421 --> 17:08.096
Yeah. Don't let the captain feel ya up!

17:13.273 --> 17:15.026
I knew you'd be out here!

17:15.569 --> 17:18.993
I brought you dinner!
You're eating, right, Andy?

17:20.078 --> 17:23.669
Quit calling me that when my men are around. Fuko.

17:24.086 --> 17:26.340
Oh, come on. Where's the harm?

17:29.639 --> 17:33.606
I just gave them the unluck ritual
a second ago. You see, Mr. Ash...

17:33.606 --> 17:35.233
Wait. Let me guess.

17:37.446 --> 17:39.199
Ash got a little dirty.

17:40.745 --> 17:43.416
Camus's chair broke and dropped him on his ass.

17:44.209 --> 17:45.963
Wow! Correct!

17:46.923 --> 17:49.679
Mr. Ash is always staring at my chest!
I can't stand it!

17:49.971 --> 17:51.683
What's so great about these things, anyway?

17:52.518 --> 17:54.814
Mr. Camus doesn't do that.

17:56.818 --> 17:58.739
Oh, hey! Is that a new brew?

17:58.989 --> 18:03.331
Yeah. Apparently it's called "Budwaiser."
It's good stuff.

18:03.331 --> 18:06.295
Then, Ms. Josh and the others must
be drinking it around now, too!

18:08.466 --> 18:09.719
Fuko.

18:09.719 --> 18:13.017
What do you think it means to die?

18:13.309 --> 18:15.313
That came out of nowhere,
what's wrong?

18:15.313 --> 18:17.025
I'm being serious over here.

18:17.944 --> 18:20.699
I personally think it's when your brain stops thinking.

18:21.283 --> 18:23.162
<i>Thinking means you can challenge.</i>

18:23.664 --> 18:25.584
<i>Thinking means you can change.</i>

18:27.547 --> 18:32.807
<i>I think when a person can't do that anymore,
that's when they're dead.</i>

18:35.019 --> 18:38.986
Hmm... I don't quite agree with that.

18:39.946 --> 18:40.614
In my opinion...

18:41.575 --> 18:46.000
...you only truly die when people stop remembering you.

18:47.169 --> 18:50.801
I lost my parents in an accident-no...

18:50.801 --> 18:55.686
I killed them with my ability by accident,
along with a bunch of other people.

18:56.521 --> 18:58.775
I thought not seeing them was their deaths.

18:59.276 --> 19:01.656
But I think it's slightly different.

19:02.783 --> 19:08.127
After all, both my mom and my dad
have always been in my heart...

19:08.712 --> 19:11.843
...constantly telling me that it wasn't my fault.

19:13.179 --> 19:16.603
And said that if I keep living,
something wonderful will happen one day.

19:19.066 --> 19:23.491
It might just be a fantasy I've created
to escape from the weight of my sins.

19:24.409 --> 19:25.286
But...

19:25.955 --> 19:29.127
My mom and dad have always helped me out-
even to this day.

19:30.380 --> 19:33.637
That's why I don't feel like they're dead yet.

19:34.639 --> 19:37.352
Of course, I can't meet them in the flesh, but...

19:38.187 --> 19:42.655
...I'm sure that Ms. Josh and the others
are alive and well inside of you, Andy.

19:44.867 --> 19:47.957
Yeah. I sure hope they are.

19:50.420 --> 19:51.046
You...

19:51.463 --> 19:57.935
You finally smiled! Boy, all that hard work
I did finally paid off. It was so worth...

19:57.935 --> 19:59.229
...it?

20:00.608 --> 20:06.578
1865. April 15. Washington, D.C.

20:07.120 --> 20:09.542
That's my oldest memory.

20:09.918 --> 20:12.757
Now that I've told you,
you'll go there, right?

20:13.341 --> 20:14.719
Huh?

20:15.053 --> 20:20.313
I'll be fine now.
So long as I don't forget, I won't ever be alone.

20:22.400 --> 20:24.530
N... no...

20:24.530 --> 20:28.872
The one I love is you,
but not you at the same time.

20:29.122 --> 20:34.216
So I don't think we should be doing th-that right now.

20:34.926 --> 20:35.678
Oh.

20:36.513 --> 20:40.144
Did I just say that I love you?

20:40.979 --> 20:47.158
Y'did. But that aside, Fuko...
you're starting to fade away.

20:47.158 --> 20:52.712
Whoa, what is this?
Am I going someplace else now? Um, um...

20:53.003 --> 20:53.880
Andy!

20:54.297 --> 20:55.341
Yeah?

20:55.592 --> 21:00.309
144 years from now!
On August 1st, 2020!

21:00.309 --> 21:03.190
We'll meet at Shinjuku Station!

21:03.650 --> 21:07.742
I'll try to run away from you!
But make sure you catch me!

21:08.325 --> 21:12.208
If you do...
on that day, I'll kiss you!

21:14.505 --> 21:16.634
So be sure not to forget!

21:16.926 --> 21:18.513
As long as you don't forget...

21:19.974 --> 21:21.811
...Then people won't die.

21:23.105 --> 21:26.236
Sick. Wicked sick.

21:37.300 --> 21:38.553
Where am I?

21:44.356 --> 21:45.859
1865

21:45.859 --> 21:47.362
APRIL 15TH

21:47.362 --> 21:49.032
WASHINGTON D.C.

21:49.032 --> 21:54.042
TO BE CONTINUED

23:24.139 --> 23:25.016
PREVIEW

23:25.099 --> 23:27.145
<i>Are memories worth protecting?</i>

23:27.604 --> 23:31.111
<i>Within differing times,
the two men finally cross paths.</i>

23:31.111 --> 23:33.365
<i>The girl's unluck envelops death.</i>

23:33.490 --> 23:37.165
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 22-Profile.</i>

23:37.248 --> 23:39.085
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
